"""The World in One Day - Sunday 22 November 2026.

A one-page newspaper front page summing up 22 November 2026 in 40 stories:
13 highlights with drawn visuals, a UTC timeline, stat boxes, a region bar,
a numbered world map, and the 27 remaining stories in a list.

Runs on the Python standard library only (os, struct, sys, zlib). All text
is set in the sample's fonts - Playfair Display 900 for the masthead and
700 for headlines, Liberation Serif for body copy, Liberation Sans Bold
for labels - baked in as 4-bit grayscale coverage bitmaps (see GLYPHS
below), rendered live from the TTFs by a dev-time generator script; at
runtime this file only decodes hex and blends each glyph pixel's coverage
between the ink colour and the background beneath it. Writes one PNG to
/output/entry.png (or to argv[1] when given), 1024x1024, under 1 MiB.
"""
